  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the project\'s scope. My goal is to revamp the entire UI for a mortgage broker\'s website. I\'ve noted that this is a multi-page endeavor, and I\'ll need to account for multiple routes and page structures in the redesign. I am working to be mindful of structural boundaries even if it conflicts with a simple architecture.\n\n\n**Considering Structural Boundaries**\n\nI am now carefully considering the explicit multi-page request. The initial rules seem to conflict with this structural requirement, but upon closer examination of the constraints, I believe the \"single-view\" limitation only applies to \"simple, short requests.\" Since this is a more involved project, the multi-page request is valid. This opens the door to using Next.js\'s App Router for a more organized `/app/about/page.tsx`, `/app/services/page.tsx` type of layout. I\'m also now analyzing the RIVO LENDING logo to begin extracting the brand\'s color palette, focusing on vibrant teal/cyan and a dark navy blue for the Tailwind theme.\n\n\n**Analyzing Visual Inspiration**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the visual aspects of the logo, noting the serif font for \"RIVO\" and sans-serif for \"LENDING\". I plan to update the fonts in `layout.tsx` to reflect this. I\'ll also be using Framer Motion for minimal animations and transitions, as I\'ve already installed `framer-motion`. I\'m also going through `https://laxmihomeloans.com.au/` for structural and component inspiration. Since I don\'t have the image path of the logo, I will focus on building the brand styling around the colors.\n\n\n**Addressing the Logo**\n\nI\'ve decided to use text for the logo, since an uploaded image path is unavailable. I\'ll represent it with a serif \"RIVO\" in teal and a sans-serif \"LENDING\" in navy. The plan is to continue designing around the teal and navy color scheme.\n\n\n**Planning the Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now outlining the component structure, including a strong headline, CTA buttons, and a \"How it works\" section. I\'ll include a services grid, a \"Why Choose Us\" section, testimonials, and a contact form with lead capture. The plan is to build a multi-page structure with `/app/page.tsx` for the home page, `/app/about/page.tsx` for \"About Us\", `/app/services/page.tsx` for \"Services\", and `/app/contact/page.tsx` for \"Contact\", along with a Navbar and Footer. I intend to refactor `layout.tsx` to add fonts (like Lora and Montserrat) and the persistent Navbar and Footer. I will rewrite `app/page.tsx` to match the brand.\n\n\n**Implementing the Architecture**\n\nI am now actively implementing the architecture. I\'m focusing on crafting the individual pages: `/app/about/page.tsx`, `/app/services/page.tsx`, and `/app/contact/page.tsx`. Styling will be handled through Tailwind, using custom color classes or close equivalents like `teal-600` and `slate-900`. I\'m integrating page transitions and fade-in-up animations using Framer Motion. I\'m taking the execution steps in order, starting with checking the current structure with `list_dir`. Then I\'ll create Navbar and Footer components, update the layout, the home page, and create the other necessary pages. I\'m refining the brand colors for use throughout the pages.\n\n\n**Refining Color and Fonts**\n\nI\'m now refining the brand\'s color palette and fonts within the project. I\'ve pinpointed the exact teal as `#00B4B6` and the navy as `#1A2E44`. I\'ve set up global CSS variables in `globals.css` using the `@theme` directive for better organization. I\'ve also established Montserrat and Lora as the sans-serif and serif fonts, respectively. I\'m actively using arbitrary values and global CSS variables. Next, I plan to integrate the Navbar and Footer into the `layout.tsx` file, along with the font configurations.\n\n\n**Constructing the Navigation**\n\nI\'m currently drafting the Navbar component with links for Home, About, Services, and Contact. The logo will be rendered as styled text: a serif \"RIVO\" in teal and a sans-serif \"LENDING\" in navy. Concurrent to this, I\'m sketching out the content for each page: Hero, \"How it works,\" Services, and so on.\n\n**Preparing Page Content**\n\nI am now focusing on the content and structure of each page, concurrently preparing the file and directory creation steps. The \"Home\" page will include a hero section, a \"How it works\" section with three steps, a services summary, testimonials, and a call to action. The \"About\" page will cover company overview, values, and team information. The services page will contain detailed service cards, and the Contact page will utilize our Zod/React Hook Form and appropriate styling. I\'ll need to use `mkdir` for directories if `create_file` cannot make them on its own, and edit `app/globals.css`, `app/layout.tsx`. I also need to make the component and page files.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 22
      nanos: 519712664
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
