  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing the New Pages**\n\nI\'m now generating the necessary files: `/app/page.tsx`, `/app/about/page.tsx`, `/app/services/page.tsx`, and `/app/contact/page.tsx`. I\'ve begun to build the content of the home page, `/app/page.tsx`, focusing on the initial framework for motion.\n\n\n**Constructing the Home Page**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `lucide-react` icons and the `next/image` component into the home page structure. My current focus is on building the service section with its four distinct offerings. I\'m leveraging the provided service data to populate this section, mapping each service title, description, and icon to their respective components.\n\n\n**Refining the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the aesthetic of the hero section. I\'ve integrated a background image and overlay to establish the visual tone. The headline is animated, creating an engaging entry. I\'m also now implementing the subtext animation and refining the button styling.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Subtext**\n\nI\'m now implementing the subtext animation with opacity and a subtle vertical shift to the hero section. I\'ve integrated a clear call to action with a \"Free Consultation\" button, complete with styling, which is linked to the contact page. I\'ve also added a link to the services.\n\n\n**Integrating the New Section**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Why Choose Us / Highlights\" section with a three-column grid. I\'m focusing on motion effects, using `motion.div` with initial opacity and vertical position to produce smooth transitions on scroll. The content consists of a list of key benefits which are populated from data.\n\n\n**Implementing the \'Why Choose Us\'**\n\nI\'ve integrated the \"Why Choose Us\" section, focusing on its visual appeal and functionality. I\'m leveraging motion effects for smooth transitions, animating the three-column grid containing our key benefits. Each section dynamically pulls in data, ensuring the content is easily managed. I\'ve also implemented the checkmark icons with their corresponding text.\n\n\n**Adding the Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the services section, pulling data to populate a grid layout. Each service entry includes a title, description, and a link to view all services. I\'m leveraging `motion.div` with staggered transitions for visual interest, applying initial opacity and vertical positioning. I\'m also ensuring the content dynamically updates.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Services**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the services section\'s visual design and functionality, making sure it\'s fully responsive, including a \"view all services\" link for mobile. I\'ve built in the animation to create a good visual experience. I\342\200\231ve incorporated the hover effects and transitions. Now I\342\200\231m just tidying things up.\n\n\n**Incorporating the Testimonials**\n\nI\'m now integrating the testimonials section into the design. I\'m focusing on a clean, visually appealing layout that prominently features client feedback. Currently, I\'m working on the responsiveness and the data integration to populate the testimonials. I want to highlight the client\'s experiences.\n\n\n**Implementing the Testimonial Content**\n\nI\'m currently working on populating the testimonials section with actual client data, formatting it to match the provided structure. Each testimonial now includes star ratings, client quotes, names, and roles, ensuring a cohesive presentation. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and smooth transitions. I\'ve used `motion.div` to animate each testimonial with a slight delay for a staggered effect, and implemented the stars.\n\n\n\n**Creating the About Page**\n\nI\'m now generating `/app/about/page.tsx`, focusing on its content and structure. I\'m starting with a hero section featuring a headline and a brief description. I\342\200\231m leveraging `motion` for initial opacity and vertical transitions to give a smooth entrance. I\'m also preparing to add other sections as required.\n\n\n**Refining the Content**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the content. I\'ve integrated a new section with text and image, ensuring the layout is visually appealing and informative. I\'m focusing on the animation of the sections with `motion.div`.\n\n\n**Adding the \'About Us\' Copy**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"About Us\" copy, focusing on a clear and concise presentation of Rivo Lending\'s core values and approach. I\'ve highlighted their industry expertise and commitment to transparency, tailoring the content to resonate with the audience. I\'ve integrated this new content into the current section.\n\n\n**Populating the Service Page**\n\nI\'m now populating the service page, specifically focusing on dynamically integrating and styling service entries. I\'m leveraging a map function to iterate through the data, ensuring each service has an appropriate title, description, and link, and is visually represented within a styled grid. I\'m also now adding some icons to each section.\n\n\n**Populating the Service Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data for each service item onto the page. I\'ve populated the page with titles, descriptions, and icons. I\'m leveraging `motion.div` with staggered transitions for visual interest, enhancing the user\'s experience. I\342\200\231m focusing on a clean and intuitive presentation.\n\n\n**Refining the Service Content**\n\nI\'m now implementing the service section on the service page, structuring the individual service entries to include a title, description, and link, all within a responsive grid layout. I\'ve focused on animating each service entry with staggered effects for visual appeal, to keep the content engaging. I\'ve also integrated the necessary data dynamically.\n\n\n**Constructing the Contact Page**\n\nI\'m now building the contact page, `/app/contact/page.tsx`, and I\'ve integrated the necessary libraries like `react-hook-form`, `zod`, and `lucide-react`. I\'m focusing on the form structure using `useForm` and data validation with Zod. I\'m preparing a contact form, ready to handle user input. I\'m also planning to integrate the contact details.\n\n\n**Validating the Form**\n\nI\'ve just implemented form validation using Zod to ensure data integrity for the contact page. I\'m leveraging the `useForm` hook with `zodResolver` to handle validation rules and error messages. I\'m also simulating an API call and creating success and loading states.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing the Contact Page**\n\nI\'m now integrating the form\'s submission state feedback: success, error, and loading. I\'ve focused on visual cues to guide the user and ensure a seamless experience. I\'m also ensuring the form responds correctly to these states with appropriate animations and messages.\n\n\n**Adding Contact Info**\n\nI\'m now integrating the contact information section into the contact page\'s design. I\'m focusing on a clean, visually distinct layout, ensuring the contact details stand out. I\'ve used a background and styling to create an appealing design. The phone number and other contact details are integrated and visually prominent.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Contact Info**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided contact information to be accessible from the contact page. I\'ve designed the page with a distinct visual layout using a background. I\'m focusing on the integration and styling of the contact details, which are now visually prominent.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the contact information directly onto the contact page. I\'ve designed the page with a separate visual section for contact details. I\'m focusing on the integration and styling of the contact details. I\'ve built in the final styling for the visual prominence of the contact information.\n\n\n**Implementing the Thank You**\n\nI\'m now integrating a thank you message that appears upon form submission on the contact page, incorporating a clear, concise display. I\'ve designed the visual elements to confirm the message\'s visibility and to maintain the overall page design. I\342\200\231m focusing on a clean, unobtrusive display to guide the user.\n\n\n**Refining the Input Fields**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the input fields for the contact form, paying attention to the styling and validation. I\'ve integrated `className` to incorporate more robust styling and enhanced the appearance. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and user-friendliness, and validation is still a key concern.\n\n\n**Enhancing the Form**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the styling and validation of specific input fields in the contact form, and I\'ve integrated `className` to incorporate more robust styling and enhanced the appearance. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and user-friendliness. I\'ve been adding the validation details too, which is an ongoing consideration.\n\n\n**Adding the Loan Purpose**\n\nI\'m now integrating a dropdown menu into the contact form to determine how I can help, which uses `react-hook-form` to register and manage it. I\'m focusing on incorporating the `loanPurpose` option, with options like \"Buying First Home\" and \"Refinancing\". I\'ve set up validation with zod to display the \"Select a service\" option.\n\n\n**Adding Loan Amount & Message**\n\nI\'m now integrating the estimated loan amount and message input fields to the contact form, using `react-hook-form` and incorporating styling and validation. I\'ve designed a structured input field with a placeholder and a text area for an enhanced user experience and have integrated them into the layout. I\'ve added validation and styling.\n\n\n"
