    thinking: "**Defining the Core Focus**\n\nI\'m currently zeroing in on defining the core focus for the RIVO Lending website redesign. It\'s becoming clearer that establishing a premium, trustworthy, and modern aesthetic is key, all while avoiding the typical finance clich\303\251s. The visual direction I\'m taking is significantly influenced by a specific visual resource I identified earlier.\n\n\n**Refining the Brand Identity**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously reviewing the new brand identity and detailed design document. The brand personality is solidifying as trustworthy, personal, and premium, with a distinct Australian touch. I\'m focusing on the color palette, especially the deep navy and RIVO teal, aiming to ensure a cohesive and modern look. Typography will feature DM Serif Display and Manrope.\n\n\n**Visualizing Website Elements**\n\nI\'m now concretely envisioning specific website elements, like the RIVO wave as an SVG curve, and the monochrome trust strip showcasing lender logos and key stats. I\'m imagining clean, whitespace-rich \"How RIVO Helps\" cards, and the impactful \"The RIVO Difference\" section with large teal numbers on a navy background. The interactive mortgage calculator is also taking shape.\n\n\n**Planning the Implementation**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the actual implementation steps, focusing on integrating the refined brand identity into the website\'s structure. I need to update `metadata.json` if needed, and definitely `app/layout.tsx` to include the fonts and Tailwind variables. Defining the new color palette using Tailwind v4 syntax in `app/globals.css` is also in progress. I\'m also planning reusable components, and am starting to rewrite `/app/page.tsx` with the 14-section flow.\n\n\n**Implementing the Style Guide**\n\nI\'m currently working on translating the style guide into code. I\'ve defined the new brand colors in Tailwind using v4 syntax, and I\'ve integrated the fonts, DM Serif Display and Manrope, into `layout.tsx`. My focus is on creating a responsive and visually appealing navbar, incorporating a scroll listener for a transparent-to-white background transition. I\'m also preparing to build the hero section with a split design, an Australian lifestyle image, and a floating card effect using `motion.div`. Finally, I am planning to implement the trust strip with lender logos and key stats.\n\n\n**Structuring the Sections**\n\nI\'m now outlining each website section, ensuring a logical flow. I\'m focusing on \"How RIVO Helps,\" with four soft-shadowed cards. \"The RIVO Difference\" will feature large teal numbers on a navy background. I am planning an intuitive calculator using native range inputs, and a journey timeline is being incorporated. I am also planning sections for the broker, success stories, testimonials, lender network, FAQ, and final CTA. Finally, I\'ll need to use `lucide-react` for icons and I\'m prepared to split the code to avoid any tool limitations.\n\n\n**Constructing the Wave**\n\nI\'m now thinking specifically about how to incorporate the \"RIVO Wave\" element. I\'m leaning toward an SVG component for use as a section divider.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m starting to follow through on the execution steps. I need a slider component, but will be using native `<input type=\"range\">`. I\'ve started editing `app/globals.css` for colors and `app/layout.tsx` for fonts and body colors. The navbar and footer components are next, but I\'m focusing now on `app/page.tsx`, deciding between one massive file or numerous separate components, leaning towards a single long file for now.\n\n\n**Designing the Logo**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the logo implementation. I can use a simpler typographic logo with the RIVO text in DM Serif Display with a teal wave underneath, as the user provided a sample logo image. I am drafting `app/globals.css` with Tailwind colors and I\'ll make the fonts available via `app/layout.tsx`. I\'ll create the Navbar and Footer components using these elements.\n\n\n**Implementing the Navbar**\n\nI\'m now focused on the Navbar. I\'ve integrated the fonts and will be setting the colors using Tailwind in `globals.css` and `layout.tsx`. I\'ve started on `Navbar.tsx` and am setting up a scroll effect for a white background, using `useState` and `useEffect` to manage the background change. I\'m also starting to structure `page.tsx`, which will include the Hero, Trust Strip, and \"How We Help\" sections.\n\n\n**Structuring the Sections**\n\nI\'m now outlining each website section, ensuring a logical flow. I\'m focusing on sections like the Mortgage Calculator, with interactive, native inputs, the Journey Timeline, Meet Your Broker, Success Stories, Testimonial, Lender Network, FAQ (featuring teal plus icons with ample whitespace), and the Final CTA. I\'m preparing to edit `app/page.tsx` with a full-file replacement, and aiming for around 400-500 lines of code. I\'ll be implementing every detail.\n\n\n**Defining Calculator and Waves**\n\nI\'m now refining the mortgage calculator\'s logic. I\'ve set up state variables for property value and deposit, calculating loan amount, LVR, and monthly repayment, including a base interest rate of 6%. I\'m incorporating a white to navy wave and a navy to white wave using SVG paths as section dividers. I\'m focusing on the white wave for the bottom, for use as a section divider.\n\n\n**Preparing the Codebase**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the codebase structure. I\'m focusing on file management, specifically planning to use `create_file` with `Overwrite: true` to fully replace critical files. I\'m preparing instructions for `app/globals.css`, `app/layout.tsx`, `components/Navbar.tsx`, `components/Footer.tsx`, and `app/page.tsx` now. I\'ll need to fetch the existing `app/page.tsx` as a reference. I am confirming that I can replace the files, so it will be safer and cleaner to proceed.\n\n\n**Confirming File Replacement**\n\nI\'m now fully preparing for file overwrites, including confirming the process and drafting the core CSS and layout files. I can confidently overwrite files now, which is great. I\'ve drafted `app/globals.css` with the brand colors and `app/layout.tsx` to handle the fonts. I\'m ready for the next files.\n\n\n**Implementing the Layout**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided code, starting with `app/layout.tsx`. I\'ve copied the code to set up the HTML structure, fonts, and the `Navbar` and `Footer` components. I\'m ensuring the layout handles the scrolling smoothly. I am now working on `components/Navbar.tsx` and incorporating the scroll effect. I am also working on creating the `Hero` section and other sections as well.\n\n\n**Constructing the Navbar**\n\nI\'m now integrating the navbar, implementing the scroll effect that I designed. I\'ve finished the scroll effect using `useState` and `useEffect` and am starting to implement the links and structure. The navbar is responsive and I\'m adding a white to transparent background transition on scroll. I\'m focusing on the component file and ready to make the next steps.\n\n\n**Implementing the Sections**\n\nI\'m now fully working on implementing the page sections. The navbar with scroll effect is implemented. I\'m building out the hero section with the RIVO logo, and the trust strip is next. I\'m focusing on the \"How RIVO Helps\" cards, followed by \"The RIVO Difference,\" and then the mortgage calculator, with interactive range inputs. My goal is for this to be a single, long file.\n\n\n**Refining the Navbar**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the navbar, making it perfect. I\'ve integrated the design, and implemented both mobile and desktop views, as well as the transition on scroll effect. I\'ve finished the links and the call-to-action button, ensuring responsiveness. The component now fully reflects the refined brand identity.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Navbar**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the mobile navbar. I am implementing the mobile dropdown design and integrating it with the desktop view, ensuring a seamless experience. My focus is on perfect responsive behavior, with the scroll effect. I am testing both the menu and desktop views, with the mobile dropdown and transition.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Mobile Navbar**\n\nI\'m now fully done with the mobile navbar. The dropdown is integrated and responsive, working perfectly with the scroll effect and desktop view. I\'ve finished the desktop and mobile menus with flawless behavior. I am ready to move on.\n\n\n**Constructing the Hero**\n\nI\'m now building the hero section, incorporating the RIVO logo and text from the design. I\'m focusing on responsiveness across devices. I am also implementing the trust strip.\n\n\n\n**Implementing the Hero and Trust**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Hero section and trust strip, focusing on a responsive design. I\'m building out both, making sure to incorporate the RIVO logo, text, and other elements.\n\n\n**Integrating the Footer**\n\nI\'m now integrating the footer, working with the existing design code. I\'m focusing on the different sections, like the links for brokers, why RIVO, testimonials, and careers, along with the resources section with calculators, guides, FAQs. I\'m also preparing for the copyright section.\n\n\n**Integrating the Footer**\n\nI\'m now integrating the footer, working with the provided code and styling for a consistent look. I\'ve focused on incorporating sections for various links and content. My attention is now on crafting a responsive and user-friendly copyright section.\n\n\n**Structuring the Sections**\n\nI\'m now outlining how the sections will flow and developing the initial skeleton code for each. I\'m focusing on the \"What We Do\" cards, \"Rivo Difference\" section, an interactive mortgage calculator with native inputs and the \"Journey\" timeline. I plan to use `lucide-react` for all the icons.\n\n\n**Adding the Floating Widget**\n\nI\'m now integrating the floating contact widget. I\'ll add the persistent widget to `app/layout.tsx` for cross-page visibility, which I can also put it in `app/page.tsx` for simplicity. I\'m focusing on refining the calculator component with property value and deposit state variables.\n\n\n**Calculating the Monthly Repayment**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided mortgage calculation logic into the component, focusing on accurate monthly repayment computation based on loan amount, interest rate, and term. I\'m also ensuring the visual design elements\342\200\224the use of whitespace, rounded corners, soft shadows, and text colors\342\200\224are implemented in the calculator interface, and in the Hero section, and trust line.\n\n\n**Implementing the Mortgage Calculator**\n\nI\'m now implementing the mortgage calculator with its functionality. I\'ve integrated the calculation logic and made sure the monthly repayment calculation works accurately, incorporating a default 6% interest rate. I\'ve also focused on implementing the visual elements for whitespace, rounded corners, soft shadows, and text colors. I\'m focusing on the native inputs for property value and deposit.\n\n\n**Adjusting the RIVO Wave**\n\nI\'m revisiting the RIVO Wave implementation, specifically for \"The RIVO Difference\" section. I\'ve realized a direct upward translation will obscure the content, so I am rethinking the positioning, considering how to adjust the SVG component for optimal visual presentation and content clarity.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Components**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the components, ensuring everything works perfectly. I\'m focusing on the integration. I am also focusing on the FAQ, with teal plus icons and the floating contact widget. I am ready to implement the given code.\n\n\n**Refining the Implementation**\n\nI\'m now making final adjustments to component imports for `lucide-react` and confirmed the correct `motion/react` import for Framer Motion. I\'m focusing on the Hero background image. I\'ve updated the `picsum.photos` link, and refined the range slider CSS with the Tailwind accent class, and I\'ll keep an eye on image source.\n\n\n**Reviewing the Journey Section**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual style of the \"Your Journey\" section, looking closely at layout, considering how to improve the horizontal lines. I\'m also preparing for the implementation of the final CTA section.\n\n\n"
