  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Addressing the Issue**\n\nI\'ve homed in on the core problem: the navbar\'s links don\'t correspond to any actual sections on the page due to missing IDs. The links are pointing to nonexistent targets which are causing the issues. I\'m focusing on adding the missing ID attributes. This seems like a straightforward fix.\n\n\n**Simplifying and Restructuring**\n\nI\'ve been working on a significant overhaul. I am now simplifying the navigation to `Services \302\267 About \302\267 Resources` with a \"Book a consultation\" call-to-action. Also, my focus is now on revising the page structure for visual hierarchy and to ensure there are only a few major sections: Hero, Services, Brand Difference, and the Final CTA. Other sections will now be visually toned down.\n\n\n**Refining Page Structure**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific page modifications. I am focusing on cleaning up the footer by adding language options. Then, I\'m working to integrate the language selection into the Hero section as well. I\'m ensuring IDs are in place for navigation, and have updated the content to match those new structures. Lastly, I\'m making sure CTAs are text links and removing the Lender Network diagram.\n\n\n**Refining Testimonial Focus**\n\nI\'m now consolidating the reviews/social proof into a single, less visually intense section. I\'ve outlined a plan to refine the `page.tsx` file in chunks. The first part replaces the hero CTA to add multilingual support. The next replaces the heavy stats and removes the Lender Network section, and I\'ll add the IDs to the services, about, and resources sections. I\'m making sure links are subtle text links where necessary. I\'m combining RIVO difference and Broker section into one \"about\" section. The calculator section will have reduced visual weight.\n\n\n**Overhauling `page.tsx`**\n\nI\'m now completely rewriting `page.tsx`. Given the extent of the changes \342\200\223 removing entire sections, adjusting visual emphasis \342\200\223 I\'ve decided to overwrite the file rather than attempting surgical edits. It\'s a cleaner approach for such a significant structural overhaul. I\'m focusing on a fresh `page.tsx` that will streamline the Hero, Services, Brand Difference, and Final CTA sections while eliminating the lender network and toning down other elements.\n\n\n**Implementing the New Structure**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the new section IDs, and I am making sure the sections align. I am adding new language options. Also, I have begun to organize the sections in the order described previously: Hero, Services, Brand Difference, Final CTA, and the toned-down supporting sections. I am focusing on making sure all links work.\n\n\n**Updating Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the visual elements. I\'ve selected new hero imagery to better reflect the target audience, replacing the placeholder. I\'m also ensuring the alt text accurately describes the image. The navigation now uses the updated links, and I\'ve added language options to the footer.\n\n\n**Executing the Edits**\n\nI\'ve determined the most efficient approach: `multi_edit_file` is the best choice for updating both `Navbar.tsx` and `Footer.tsx`. For `Navbar.tsx`, I\'ll replace the home loans and refinance links with the new structure. Also, I will be changing the CTA text to \"Book a consultation.\" I will create a new `page.tsx` file from scratch since there is a substantial layout rewrite, which will allow me to restructure the hierarchy.\n\n\n**Finalizing Nav and Footer**\n\nI am now focusing on the final tweaks. I have updated the call-to-action on the navbar, and completed edits for the footer, incorporating new language options. I am making final adjustments to the navigation links.\n\n\n**Integrating Language Selection**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the language indicator into `Footer.tsx`. The goal is to add the language selector to the existing contact link within the footer. I\'ve confirmed the structure and am drafting the new `page.tsx` file from scratch.\n\n\n**Adding Language Indicators**\n\nI\'m now integrating the language selection within the Hero section, aiming for clear visual consistency. I\'m focusing on the implementation details using Tailwind, ensuring the language indicators are functional and visually appealing, incorporating flags as well. I\'m prioritizing accessibility and responsiveness across all devices.\n\n\n**Incorporating Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating a high-quality Unsplash image `https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512917774080-9991f1c4c750?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=1600` into the Hero section to enhance visual appeal and convey trust. I\'ve designed a \"Restrained Trust Strip\" section, a quiet credibility section with lender and experience metrics, to build trust. I will use the code provided.\n\n\n**Implementing Trust Section**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided \"Restrained Trust Strip\" code, modifying it to match the rest of the visual style. I\'m focusing on making the section visually subdued and non-intrusive. I am also working on adding the new service and about sections\' id attributes. Finally, I\'ll review and ensure the section is properly structured within the `page.tsx` file.\n\n\n**Rewriting `page.tsx`**\n\nI\'m now rewriting the `page.tsx` file from scratch with a renewed focus on the structure. I\'m consolidating the \"Brand Difference\" and \"Broker\" sections into a unified block. I\'m focusing on incorporating the three CTA placements: primary \"Book a consultation\" in the hero, a contextual text link below the calculator, and the final \"Book a consultation.\" I\'m ensuring all sections are visually balanced. I\'m making sure all the id attributes and links match.\n\n\n"
