  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Eliminating Irrelevant Content**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the user\'s explicit directive: remove the \"How much could you borrow?\" calculator. It\'s a clear exclusion, and I\'m prioritizing that removal to ensure the response aligns with the user\'s specific request. Focus is now directed on understanding the remaining aspects of the prompt.\n\n\n**Refining Homepage Structure**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the homepage based on the Luxe Finance Group reference, emphasizing a clear user progression. I\'m thinking in terms of \"What do you need? \342\206\222 Here\'s what we do \342\206\222 Why trust us \342\206\222 Let\'s connect\". I\'m also planning a hero section with editorial copy, and two clear pathways. Service cards will focus on simple visual entry points with a one-sentence value proposition, with links to specific service pages like `/services/home-loans`. I\'m moving toward an \"About/Trust\" section, and a tight FAQ of genuinely important questions.\n\n\n**Structuring Homepage Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of `/app/page.tsx`, starting with the removal of calculator-related state variables. The hero section is next for reworking, specifically targeting direct headlines and revised CTAs. I\'m keeping the trust strip as is, and the focus shifts to updating service entry cards, ensuring clear, concise value propositions and hrefs to relevant service pages.\n\n\n**Updating Service Descriptions**\n\nI\'m now revising the service descriptions, making sure each one clearly articulates a value proposition. I\'m focusing on concise messaging for Refinance, Investment, and Build & Renovate options, like: \"See if your current loan is still working for you and structure a better rate,\" for example. The goal is to provide immediate clarity, and I\'m updating the button text to progress users. I\'m also preparing a \"Brand Difference\" section that will highlight our audience specialization, and then the calculator section will get the axe. Finally, I\'ll keep just a few key FAQ questions, and add a link to see all.\n\n\n**Implementing Service Links**\n\nI\'ve just added the `/services/slug` links to the `helpCards` array as requested, ensuring users are directed to the correct service pages. Now, I\'m moving on to the hero section, the brand difference text, and of course, the removal of the calculator section. I\'ll wrap up by adding a \"View all FAQs\" link to the FAQ section. I\'ve also removed all state variables related to the calculator as a first step. I\'ve adjusted imports and I am now ready to move onto the next component in the process.\n\n\n**Refining Headline Messaging**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the hero section\'s headline and description to align with Luxe Finance Group\'s approach. I\'ve switched the header to \"Your priority is finding the right loan. Ours is making it happen.\" and updated the paragraph to speak to buying, refinancing, or building. The goal is directness, clarity, and quick value proposition. I\'m focusing on ensuring it is relevant for each service, and provides a clear user entrypoint.\n\n\n**Adjusting Home Page Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the user\'s feedback by keeping the ZIP\'s calm design, but adapting the Luxe architecture. I\'ve updated the hero section headline and button text to \"Buy a Property\" and \"Refinance\". I\'ve also swapped out the `<p>` elements inside help cards for `<Link>` elements, ensuring users are directed to the correct service pages. The \"About/Brand Difference\" section is being updated to reflect Luxe\'s audience focus and dedicated expert approach. Finally, I\'ve removed the calculator section as per the instructions.\n\n\n"
