  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Homepage Overhaul**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on a significant homepage restructure for `Rivo`, informed by the `Finora` analysis. The goal is to reshape the core layout based on `Finora`\'s compositional insights while retaining `Rivo`\'s brand. That means calm, sharp aesthetics, no fintech gradients, etc. The most immediate priority is a stronger, more consistent sizing hierarchy for the hero section and subsequent modules.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Hierarchy**\n\nI\'ve been refining the homepage\'s visual hierarchy, specifically for the hero section and subsequent modules. Focusing on editorial scale for major sections with large headings and ample whitespace, as well as utility scale for functional, tighter components. Section spacing now ranges from 110-160px. Large feature padding is being set at 40-56px.\n\n\n**Refining Component-Driven Architecture**\n\nMy current focus is on the implementation architecture, refining a component-driven structure for the homepage redesign. I\'m prioritizing components like `SectionLabel`, `SectionHeading`, `ScrollReveal`, and `ImageReveal`, and deciding whether to keep them local or abstract. I\'m also ensuring a smoother offset grid and a more editorial, less SaaS-like feel. I\'m planning to make forms and CTAs larger, with only one primary action per visual area.\n\n\n**Implementing Page Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on the `app/page.tsx` overhaul, removing the old structure and implementing custom components like `Reveal`, `ImageReveal`, and `SectionHeading`. I\'m starting with the Hero section: huge spacing, compelling text, and an image composition with a background shape, a house/people image, and a floating trust card. Next, I\'ll build the Trust Strip section, focusing on a dark, branded design with key metrics.\n\n\n**Constructing Lending Pathways**\n\nI\'m now building out the Lending Pathways section with an asymmetric grid, focusing on \"Buy a Property,\" \"Refinance,\" and \"Invest.\" Each pathway will feature text at the top and a large image below. I\'m also working on a \"Quiet Editorial\" section with ample whitespace, using the statement \"A mortgage isn\'t one decision. It\'s a series of decisions.\" The offset grid for \"Why Rivo\" is next, followed by a human proof section.\n\n\n"
