  planner_response {
    response: "I have fully rebuilt the homepage according to your Finora-inspired composition strategy. The design now takes the scale, structure, layering, and motion principles from Finora and applies them to Rivo\342\200\231s calm, editorial brand identity.\n\nHere is a summary of the accomplishments:\n- **Hero Composition Architecture**: The hero is no longer a split column of text beside an image. It is now a fully constructed visual scene occupying the bottom half of the space. It features a massive background architectural shape in Rivo\'s warm neutral color, a large floating lifestyle photograph with an ambient continuous 8-second slow drift, and an unobtrusive overlapping credibility card.\n- **Enhanced Sizing System**: The layout spacing is no longer uniform. The hero top padding sits at a generous `192px` (`pt-48`), dropping down into `128px` section rhythms. The primary display fonts have been significantly scaled up (reaching up to `72px`), establishing a much starker contrast with the readable body copy.\n- **Large Photographic Pathways**: The generic 4-card icon grid has been completely replaced. The lending pathways (First Home, Refinancing, Investment, Construction) are now presented as two rows of asymmetric editorial cards (`42%` / `58%` splits), with the text leading on top and dominant lifestyle photography anchored to the bottom.\n- **Offset Grid Value Proposition**: The *Why Rivo* section now utilizes the Finora masonry offset layout, but stripped of the heavy SaaS drop shadows. The cards feature sharp borders, generous whitespace padding, and clean hover state reveals, all offset vertically to create an intentionally designed, imperfect column flow.\n- **Calibrated Motion System**: The animations are no longer applied blanketly across every element. Entrance transitions fire via GSAP-style scroll staggers with a `0.6s\342\200\2231s` duration and spring easing, while only the large hero photography receives the continuous ambient \"drift\" animation to keep the page feeling alive without overwhelming the user.\n- **Physically Larger CTAs**: The buttons across the site have been scaled to `56px-64px` in height with expansive horizontal padding, prioritizing a single, confident primary action in each visual zone."
    modified_response: "I have fully rebuilt the homepage according to your Finora-inspired composition strategy. The design now takes the scale, structure, layering, and motion principles from Finora and applies them to Rivo\342\200\231s calm, editorial brand identity.\n\nHere is a summary of the accomplishments:\n- **Hero Composition Architecture**: The hero is no longer a split column of text beside an image. It is now a fully constructed visual scene occupying the bottom half of the space. It features a massive background architectural shape in Rivo\'s warm neutral color, a large floating lifestyle photograph with an ambient continuous 8-second slow drift, and an unobtrusive overlapping credibility card.\n- **Enhanced Sizing System**: The layout spacing is no longer uniform. The hero top padding sits at a generous `192px` (`pt-48`), dropping down into `128px` section rhythms. The primary display fonts have been significantly scaled up (reaching up to `72px`), establishing a much starker contrast with the readable body copy.\n- **Large Photographic Pathways**: The generic 4-card icon grid has been completely replaced. The lending pathways (First Home, Refinancing, Investment, Construction) are now presented as two rows of asymmetric editorial cards (`42%` / `58%` splits), with the text leading on top and dominant lifestyle photography anchored to the bottom.\n- **Offset Grid Value Proposition**: The *Why Rivo* section now utilizes the Finora masonry offset layout, but stripped of the heavy SaaS drop shadows. The cards feature sharp borders, generous whitespace padding, and clean hover state reveals, all offset vertically to create an intentionally designed, imperfect column flow.\n- **Calibrated Motion System**: The animations are no longer applied blanketly across every element. Entrance transitions fire via GSAP-style scroll staggers with a `0.6s\342\200\2231s` duration and spring easing, while only the large hero photography receives the continuous ambient \"drift\" animation to keep the page feeling alive without overwhelming the user.\n- **Physically Larger CTAs**: The buttons across the site have been scaled to `56px-64px` in height with expansive horizontal padding, prioritizing a single, confident primary action in each visual zone."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
