  planner_response {
    response: "I apologize for the interruption! I have fully completed the Finora-inspired composition rebuild for the Rivo homepage, and I\'ve also resolved a few strict React quotation linting errors in the process. The build is perfectly green and the app is ready for preview.\n\nHere is a summary of the accomplishments to bring that premium editorial feel to life:\n\n- **Hero Composition Architecture**: The hero is no longer a generic split column. It is now a layered visual environment occupying the lower half of the space. It features a massive background architectural shape in Rivo\'s warm neutral color, a large authentic lifestyle photograph with a slow 8-second ambient drift, and an unobtrusive overlapping information card.\n- **Enhanced Sizing System**: The layout spacing is no longer uniform. The hero top padding starts with a generous `192px`, dropping down into `128px` rhythmic sections. The display typography has been significantly scaled up (reaching up to `72px`), establishing stark, confident contrast with the readable body copy.\n- **Large Photographic Pathways**: The generic 4-card icon grid was completely replaced. The lending pathways (First Home, Refinancing, Investment, Construction) are now presented as two rows of asymmetric editorial cards (e.g., `42%` / `58%` splits), with text leading on top and dominant lifestyle photography anchored to the bottom.\n- **Offset Grid Value Proposition**: The *Why Rivo* section now utilizes the Finora masonry offset layout, but stripped of the heavy SaaS drop shadows. The cards feature sharp borders, generous whitespace padding, and clean hover state reveals, all offset vertically to create an intentionally designed, imperfect column flow.\n- **Calibrated Motion System**: Animations are no longer blanket-applied. Entrance transitions fire via GSAP-style scroll staggers with a `0.6s\342\200\2231s` duration and spring easing, while only the large hero photography receives the continuous ambient \"drift\" animation to keep the page feeling alive without overwhelming the user.\n- **Substantial CTAs**: The buttons across the site have been scaled to `56px-64px` in height with expansive horizontal padding, prioritizing a single, confident primary action in each visual zone."
    modified_response: "I apologize for the interruption! I have fully completed the Finora-inspired composition rebuild for the Rivo homepage, and I\'ve also resolved a few strict React quotation linting errors in the process. The build is perfectly green and the app is ready for preview.\n\nHere is a summary of the accomplishments to bring that premium editorial feel to life:\n\n- **Hero Composition Architecture**: The hero is no longer a generic split column. It is now a layered visual environment occupying the lower half of the space. It features a massive background architectural shape in Rivo\'s warm neutral color, a large authentic lifestyle photograph with a slow 8-second ambient drift, and an unobtrusive overlapping information card.\n- **Enhanced Sizing System**: The layout spacing is no longer uniform. The hero top padding starts with a generous `192px`, dropping down into `128px` rhythmic sections. The display typography has been significantly scaled up (reaching up to `72px`), establishing stark, confident contrast with the readable body copy.\n- **Large Photographic Pathways**: The generic 4-card icon grid was completely replaced. The lending pathways (First Home, Refinancing, Investment, Construction) are now presented as two rows of asymmetric editorial cards (e.g., `42%` / `58%` splits), with text leading on top and dominant lifestyle photography anchored to the bottom.\n- **Offset Grid Value Proposition**: The *Why Rivo* section now utilizes the Finora masonry offset layout, but stripped of the heavy SaaS drop shadows. The cards feature sharp borders, generous whitespace padding, and clean hover state reveals, all offset vertically to create an intentionally designed, imperfect column flow.\n- **Calibrated Motion System**: Animations are no longer blanket-applied. Entrance transitions fire via GSAP-style scroll staggers with a `0.6s\342\200\2231s` duration and spring easing, while only the large hero photography receives the continuous ambient \"drift\" animation to keep the page feeling alive without overwhelming the user.\n- **Substantial CTAs**: The buttons across the site have been scaled to `56px-64px` in height with expansive horizontal padding, prioritizing a single, confident primary action in each visual zone."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
