  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Potential Platform Bugs**\n\nI\'m now suspecting the issue isn\'t in my code directly. I\'m focusing on whether AI Studio has a rendering bug related to `next build` that\'s surfacing the error. I didn\'t see it before I fixed those JSX errors. I\'m looking at platform-level issues now.\n\n\n**Investigating `fetch` Interception**\n\nI\'ve gone down a rabbit hole into `fetch` interception. I\'m starting to think Next.js\'s attempts to patch `window.fetch` for features like the dev overlay or App Router prefetching might be clashing with AI Studio\'s environment, where `fetch` seems to have a getter but not a setter. That\'s a good lead!\n\n\n**Unraveling `fetch` Conflicts**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a potential conflict. It seems both AI Studio and Next.js intercept `fetch`, but in different contexts. I\'m focusing on whether Next.js\'s production patching of `fetch`, specifically in `next/dist/client/app-index.js`, is the core culprit. I\'m exploring if there\'s a way to define `window.fetch` to prevent the overwrite, considering script execution order. I\'m testing redefining fetch within the root layout, before Next.js loads to control this.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 21
      nanos: 306835560
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
