  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Fetch Issues**\n\nI\'m now digging deeper into why `fetch` might be causing problems. The suspicious bit is that Next.js might be patching it. My line of thought is that it includes a `fetch` polyfill, and I\'m currently trying to pinpoint the exact error within the Next.js source code or build output. I\'m focusing on the polyfills injected into the entrypoint, specifically `next/dist/build/polyfills/fetch`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Polyfill Conflicts**\n\nI\'ve discovered the root cause is likely a conflict between Next.js\'s `whatwg-fetch` polyfill and the sandboxed environment\'s pre-defined `window.fetch`. Next.js tries to overwrite the existing `fetch`, but it fails because the sandbox has set `configurable: false`. Now I\'m exploring ways to prevent Next.js from injecting this polyfill in the first place, or, if that\'s impossible, how to gracefully handle the error. I\'m investigating redefining `window.fetch` with a setter in `app/layout.tsx`. Also, I am checking for unexpected client-side bundling of `@google/genai` which also uses `whatwg-fetch`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 194737373
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
